Dennis typicalippa says he's the  happiest man in the world he's an elder  of the manupi clan one of the  traditional owners of tiwi islands off  Australia's North Coast and on Wednesday  they won what's being described as a  David vs Goliath Court battle against a  major oil and gas company  Mr typicalippa complains that he and  other traditional owners of the tiwi  islands  was not consulted  the judge quashed the approval of a 3.6  billion project by Santos limited to  drill for gas about 140 kilometers off  the tiwi islands he said the regulator  couldn't have been reasonably satisfied  the company had carried out the  necessary consultations  last month the judge traveled to the  islands and heard firsthand about the  indigenous group's spiritual connections  to the land and sea  and the hunting and Gathering activities  passed down from their ancestors  carry on that tradition  Al to our kids and hope that they can  sort of continue on that Journey  Santos had argued the tiwi Islanders  weren't relevant stakeholders in the  project so didn't need to be involved in  talks Dennis disagreed respect  it's all a better respect for me you  know it's really disappointing that they  never came to us enough face to face  it's been a controversial case with  protests by indigenous activists outside  Court in the lead-up to the decision  they're destroying the Earth  we are the cultural Giants we're the  original people from this land the  lawyer says the ruling is Monumental and  could have not only local but Global  implications for how big companies  engage with First Nations groups  there's lots of work to be done there's  a lot of um you know proposed gas  projects in the territory and uh it's  absolutely the case that the fight  doesn't end  drilling has been suspended for now  while Santos decides whether to appeal  or put in a new application the company  says it's disappointed with the decision  calling it damaging to investor  confidence but the manupi clan is still  celebrating Dennis says he did it for  his ancestors alexio Brian Al Jazeera
 

